1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,850
Some pages need to change while they are open.

2
00:00:03,850 --> 00:00:08,125
The SignalR module gives every module of an Orchard Core site one shared

3
00:00:08,125 --> 00:00:13,497
way to host hubs, and the Redis and Azure backplanes carry their messages between instances.

4
00:00:13,497 --> 00:00:15,470
This video shows how it works.

5
00:00:20,070 --> 00:00:24,226
SignalR keeps a connection open between the browser and the server, so the

6
00:00:24,226 --> 00:00:27,394
server can send a message the moment something changes.

7
00:00:27,394 --> 00:00:30,355
A hub is the class that receives these connections.

8
00:00:30,355 --> 00:00:33,680
The Media Library and the Workflows designer each use one.

9
00:00:34,430 --> 00:00:39,958
The SignalR module registers SignalR once for the tenant, and provides the JavaScript

10
00:00:39,958 --> 00:00:42,206
client as the signalr resource.

11
00:00:42,206 --> 00:00:48,038
Backplanes relay messages between instances, and come in separate Redis and Azure modules.

12
00:00:48,038 --> 00:00:52,290
A module that hosts a hub maps it and sets its own access rules.

13
00:00:56,528 --> 00:00:59,254
In Tools, Features, search for SignalR.

14
00:00:59,254 --> 00:01:05,068
The SignalR module provides the SignalR feature, while SignalR Redis Backplane and SignalR

15
00:01:05,068 --> 00:01:08,641
Azure Backplane each come from a module of their own.

16
00:01:08,641 --> 00:01:11,548
Media SignalR comes from the Media module.

17
00:01:12,027 --> 00:01:14,232
SignalR has no pages of its own.

18
00:01:14,232 --> 00:01:16,669
A feature that hosts a hub needs it.

19
00:01:16,669 --> 00:01:21,718
Both backplanes depend on SignalR, and the Redis backplane also depends on Redis,

20
00:01:21,718 --> 00:01:23,807
as the dependency badges show.

21
00:01:24,350 --> 00:01:26,703
Let's enable SignalR Redis Backplane.

22
00:01:26,703 --> 00:01:30,972
Enabling a feature also enables the features it depends on, and the page

23
00:01:30,972 --> 00:01:33,490
confirms that the backplane was enabled.

24
00:01:37,730 --> 00:01:42,537
When Media SignalR is enabled, the Media Library connects to a hub.

25
00:01:42,537 --> 00:01:47,280
Here are two tabs of Media, Library, both showing the same folder.

26
00:01:47,746 --> 00:01:52,020
In the second tab, let's open the menu of a file, choose Rename,

27
00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:54,706
type another file name, and select Ok.

28
00:01:55,945 --> 00:01:59,623
Back in the first tab, the list shows the renamed file, and the

29
00:01:59,623 --> 00:02:01,115
page was not reloaded.

30
00:02:01,115 --> 00:02:04,900
The Media module sent a message to the hub, and the library asked

31
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:06,765
for the folder's files again.

32
00:02:10,965 --> 00:02:13,432
A hub is a class that derives from Hub.

33
00:02:13,432 --> 00:02:17,982
The Workflows hub carries the Authorize attribute with a policy name, and its

34
00:02:17,982 --> 00:02:22,915
module registers that policy so that it requires the permission to manage workflows.

35
00:02:23,665 --> 00:02:28,809
Media SignalR lists the SignalR feature as a dependency in its manifest.

36
00:02:28,809 --> 00:02:35,403
Workflows uses RequireFeatures, which runs its real-time startup only when SignalR is enabled.

37
00:02:35,403 --> 00:02:39,095
In both, the startup class maps the hub to a path.

38
00:02:39,845 --> 00:02:44,376
Options for one hub are configured with HubOptions of that hub's type, such

39
00:02:44,376 --> 00:02:46,221
as the keep-alive interval.

40
00:02:46,221 --> 00:02:49,465
Options for every hub use HubOptions without a type.

41
00:02:53,665 --> 00:02:55,983
Clients call the public methods of a hub.

42
00:02:55,983 --> 00:03:00,371
The media hub's SubscribePath method checks the user's permission for a folder, and

43
00:03:00,371 --> 00:03:03,625
then adds the connection to a group named after that folder.

44
00:03:04,375 --> 00:03:07,431
Code outside the hub sends through the hub context.

45
00:03:07,431 --> 00:03:11,666
This media event handler sends a MediaChanged message to the group of the

46
00:03:11,666 --> 00:03:15,365
parent folder, so only browsers showing that folder receive it.

47
00:03:19,565 --> 00:03:24,980
In a server-rendered view, load the client with a script tag that names the signalr resource.

48
00:03:24,980 --> 00:03:29,247
A script that opens a connection declares that it depends on signalr, so

49
00:03:29,247 --> 00:03:31,325
the client is on the page first.

50
00:03:32,075 --> 00:03:36,271
A bundled app, such as the Media gallery, includes the client in its

51
00:03:36,271 --> 00:03:39,049
own bundle and does not load this resource.

52
00:03:39,049 --> 00:03:44,265
The gallery connects to the media hub and calls SubscribePath for the folder it shows.

53
00:03:48,465 --> 00:03:52,186
A hub keeps its connections in the memory of one instance.

54
00:03:52,186 --> 00:03:56,720
With two instances behind a load balancer, a message sent on one reaches

55
00:03:56,720 --> 00:04:01,545
only the browsers connected to it, unless a backplane relays it to the other.

56
00:04:02,295 --> 00:04:06,502
The Redis backplane reuses the connection string of the Redis module.

57
00:04:06,502 --> 00:04:11,381
Each tenant's messages use their own channel prefix, made of the instance prefix,

58
00:04:11,381 --> 00:04:15,475
the tenant name and SignalR, so tenants can share one Redis server.

59
00:04:16,225 --> 00:04:20,372
The Azure SignalR Service backplane has its own connection string.

60
00:04:20,372 --> 00:04:25,670
The optional application name separates deployments that share one service, and a hash

61
00:04:25,670 --> 00:04:28,895
of the tenant name is added to keep tenants apart.

62
00:04:29,645 --> 00:04:31,967
Enable one backplane per tenant.

63
00:04:31,967 --> 00:04:37,282
If both are enabled and configured, one of them logs an error and stays inactive.

64
00:04:37,282 --> 00:04:43,635
A backplane without its connection string stays inactive too, and SignalR keeps working in memory.

65
00:04:45,635 --> 00:04:50,244
The SignalR module registers SignalR once for the tenant, and the Redis and

66
00:04:50,244 --> 00:04:53,658
Azure backplanes carry hub messages between instances.

67
00:04:53,658 --> 00:04:57,356
Your modules map their hubs and set their own access rules.

68
00:04:57,356 --> 00:04:58,835
Thanks for watching.

